 "summary": {
  "mechanism": "Per-tensor uint8 activation scales on the expand-conv output (SiLU input) and SiLU output (depthwise input) are set by one or two outlier channels (stem: ch3, range 169 at conv out / 82 at SiLU out). Most channels get 20-40 levels, and 9/32 get fewer than 6 (ch13 lives entirely in the SiLU negative lobe [-0.27,-0.10] and gets 0.5 levels: every value becomes 0 or -0.348). A depthwise conv cannot average error over channels, and its BN-folded weights are largest on exactly those small channels (ch13 sum|w|=325 vs median ~3), so the rounding error is amplified about 26 dB in features.1 and 10-24 dB in every one of the 16 depthwise convs. Weight quantization (42.7 dB), bias quantization (51.5 dB), Sigmoid output quantization (+1.8pp when removed) and a DC or negative-lobe bias (0.6% of error energy) are ruled out.",
